  "sentence": "Model (`node model.mjs`, every assumption is a flag): starting from today's 20%, when the buyback reaches half of net issuance depends on how fast Intents' growth fades: in 2027-Q2 (2 quarters) if the measured 1.87× per 90 days never fades, and never with no further growth (it stays at 20%). In between: halving every 2 quarters (the default flag), in 2027-Q3 (3 quarters); halving about every 0.9 quarters (the fade a two-point fit to the measured quarters implies, see below), not within 10 years. A scenario, not a forecast. The measured quarter-on-quarter growth went 5.8× → 6.8× → 1.7× → 0.7× → 1.2× → 1.9×; fading from the oldest quarter to the latest four implies a half-life of about 0.9 quarters, but the last 2 quarters re-accelerated (0.7× → 1.2× → 1.9×), so one steady fade fits this series poorly: that half-life is a two-point fit, and the sensitivity grid (`node model.mjs`, and the dashboard's model section) shows how much the choice matters. The bought-back NEAR sits in a multisig (held, not burned); `--resold` models some of it returning to market. If HSP-029 (max issuance 2.5% → 1.6% over 24 months; House of Stake vote 99.97% for, timelock until 2026-11-16; no start date set) began its ramp now: at the 2-quarter default, in 2027-Q3 (3 quarters); at the two-point-fit fade, in 2028-Q1 (5 quarters)."
 },
